The upstream project provides the base SaaS short-link system (admin console API,
short-link project service, gateway, aggregation entry, Vue console). This repository
is an independent, modified distribution of that work and is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or maintained by the upstream author.

Modifications made in this repository relative to the upstream baseline
(see README.md and IMPROVEMENTS.md for details and evidence):

  * Access statistics pipeline redesigned: the Redis Stream based pipeline was
    replaced with an Apache RocketMQ based one (idempotent consumption,
    backlog and duplicate-delivery behaviour measured and documented).
  * Two-level click attribution added: channel (utm_source) and campaign
    (utm_campaign) dimensions are captured, normalised, stored in a dedicated
    pre-aggregated table and exposed through the statistics APIs.
  * Redirect availability hardening: statistics messages are produced
    asynchronously with a bounded compensation queue and a circuit breaker, so a
    failing or unavailable broker no longer affects the redirect response.
  * Reproducible local development environment (no Docker/Nacos required) and a
    JMeter based load-testing setup with archived results and documented limits.
  * Rebranding and clean-up: package namespace renamed to com.linkflow.shortlink,
    build metadata, documentation and console branding unified under LinkFlow,
    third-party and upstream promotional material removed from the source tree.

